course: dictionary
lesson: 9858
title: Sympathy and its meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sympathy is a feeling of being sorry for someone who is sad, hurt or in trouble, and showing that you care. You can feel sympathy for a friend who is ill, or for someone who has lost a pet.
explain: Read the words around it to find its meaning. Oisin in Cork said his dog had died to get more time, and the teacher sent a sympathy card home. A sympathy card shows that someone cares about how you feel, so the teacher was being kind to Oisin.
explain: Sympathy can also mean agreeing with someone's side. «I have some sympathy with his view» means you understand his view and partly support it. In formal writing, «sympathies» are the kind words sent after a death, as in «with deepest sympathy».
fact: Sympathy is a noun, and it is usually uncountable: say «some sympathy», not «a sympathy».
fact: «Sympathies» is the plural, used for the kind words sent when someone has died.
fact: «At rest» is written on graves and in sympathy cards, and it means the person has died.
fact: Useful phrases: feel sympathy for, have sympathy with, out of sympathy.
fact: A sympathy card is sent to show you care when someone is sad, ill or has died.
exercise: «Oisin's teacher sent a sympathy card home.» What does sympathy show here? | Fear of the dark | *Feeling sorry and caring about Oisin | Anger about late homework | Joy at a party
exercise: «I have some sympathy with his view.» What does this mean? | *Agreeing with, or supporting, his view in part | Being very angry with his view | Asking him to write a card | Forgetting what he said
exercise: Which sentence uses sympathy correctly? | She showed me a sympathies when I was ill. | She gave a sympathy to me when I was ill. | *She showed me some sympathy when I was ill.
test: «With deepest sympathy» is written in a card. When would you see these words? | On a menu in a café | On a sign outside a shop | On a birthday card for a friend | *In a card sent after someone has died
test: In «feel sympathy for someone in trouble», which word is closest in meaning to sympathy? | Joy | Anger | Boredom | *Care
exam: Which phrase best explains sympathy? | Excitement about a party | Anger at a broken rule | Fear of the dark | *Feeling sorry for someone in trouble and caring
